rially sectioned  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm firm  white gray ill defined mass  It is located in the upper outer quadrant of the breast  5 5cm from the closest posterior margin and 2 1cm from the closest anterior margin  The rest of the parenchyma shows predominantly fatty tissue with few fibrous areas containing blue domed cysts which range from REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm in average diameter  No other suspicious lesions are identified  Representative sections of the lesion with closest margin are submitted in cassettes C F  Representative sections of breast parenchyma away from the lesion are submitted in cassettes G and H  Also received in the same container is a 10 0x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  Upon dissection of the specimen twelve possible lymph nodes are identified ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 7cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are submitted as follows  I L  one serially sectioned lymph node  M O  one serially sectioned lymph node  P  one bisected lymph node  Q R  one serially sectioned lymph node  S T  one bisected lymph node  U  one bisected lymph node  V  one serially sectioned lymph node  W  one bisected lymph node  X  one trisected lymph node  Y  two lymph nodes  Z  one serially sectioned lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm oval portion of fibroadipose tissue  surfaced by an ellipse of tan wrinkled skin  including nipple areolar complex  which measures REMOVED_DATE x 7 8cm  The specimen is not oriented  The margin is inked black and serially sectioned  The breast parenchyma has approximately 40  fibrous tissue and 60  adipose tissue  There are multiple bluish cystic areas which range from REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm in diameter  Representative sections of fibrous tissue are submitted in cassettes AA JJ  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary tissue 