Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 40 CLINICAL DATA  History of left breast cancer  Status post left breast mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL   1  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  60   REMOVED_DATE CM  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  40   EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  MICROCYST  FIBROSIS AND FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be performed  and the results reported in an addendum  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL   2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  MICROCYSTS  FIBROSIS  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND LUMINAL MICROCALCIFICATIONS  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE GROSS INTRA  OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL SPECIMEN   1   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  Right breast   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of fatty tissue with localizing wire  Sectioning reveals fat and a small amount of rubbery  white tissue  which focally forms a poorly circumscribed nodule  0 7cm in diameter  The specimen is entirely submitted in A   E  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm unremarkable breast fragment with localizing needle in place  which is entirely submitted in F   J with area corresponding to calcification in G and H  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   1   BIOPSY  NO DISCRETE LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   2   BIOPSY  NO AREA GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MEDIAL  1 PART B  RIGHT BREAST LATERAL  2   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 28 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST CANCER  SHORT STITCH SUPERIOR  LONG STITCH LATERAL    RE EXCISION  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR MARGIN   SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Note  The residual invasive carcinoma is adjacent to the healing biopsy site  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MEDIAL TISSUE   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 36                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate specimens  Labeled  left breast cancer  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral   is an oriented portion of breast  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm with an overlying ellipse of skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  There is a longitudinal scar on the skin  measuring 2 5cm  There is short and long stitch present on the specimen  The deep margin is inked black  the superior margin is inked green  the inferior margin is inked red  and the anterior margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned medial to lateral  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm  white  well defined nodule abutting the inferior deep margin  SECTION CODE  A B  medial margins of the specimen  Representative sections from medial to latera  including the well defined nodule  submitted in cassettes A through J  Labeled  left breast  additional medial tissue with the short stitch designating superior margin and the long stitch designating the new medial margin   is a portion of breast  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm with two stitch  one long and one short  The anterior portion is inked blue  the deep margin is inked black  the superior margin is inked green  and the inferior margin is inked red  The specimen is serially sectioned medial to lateral  The entire tissue is quite firm and white  Entirely submitted in from medial to lateral in cassettes K through S  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE 