 was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm breast excision specimen  The entire surface is inked black with the deep  posterior  margin overinked blue  and the superior margin overinked red  Serially sectioning the tissue reveals a hemorrhagic area  surrounded by an ill defined stellate  white  firm mass  with maximum diameter of 1 0cm  located in the center of the specimen  with fibrous extensions approaching the margins  The tissue away from this mass is almost entirely yellow fatty tissue with minimal fibrous strands  SECTION CODE A  FX  1  mass with superior margin  B  FX  2  mass with superficial margin  C  FX  3  mass with inferior margin  D  FX  4  mass with deep margin  E H  Remainder of the mass  I  Representative section of remainder of tissue  Designated  left breast  additional breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 1 5cm breast tissue  oriented by a short and long stitch designating the deep margin  two short stitches designating the medial margin  and two long stitches designating the superior margin  The entire excised surface is inked black with the superficial half overinked blue  Cross sectioning reveals an ill defined firm  white  fibrous areas abutting the superficial margin along a broad front  in the medial portion of the specimen  and focally abutting the new deep margin  Representative sections are submitted from medial to l