n  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nodular fatty tissue fragment which is bivalved and one half is frozen as FX 1  now as A  The remaining half is submitted in cassette B  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast reexcision  is a 2 8x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm ovoid fragment of breast tissue  The lateral margin is inked black and the medial margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a vague nodularity involving the entire breast tissue  No definite masses  nodules or cysts are identified  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  Section code  C E  superficial segments of tissue submitted from superior to inferior F H  deep portions of tissue submitted from superior to inferior  I J  superior and inferior poles en face respectively  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary nodes  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue from which are multiple lymph nodes ranging from 0 2cm to 3 0cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes K P  Resident  VIKRAM DESHPANDE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGN