Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 22 CLINICAL DATA  Lesion highly suspicious for carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WITH SOME FEATURES OF MEDULLARY CARCINOMA AND EXTENSIVE INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    COMEDO TYPE  SEE NOTE   Note  Infiltrating and intraductal carcinoma are present adjacent to the inked resection margins  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  The invasive tumor measures approximately 1 3cm and the ductal carcinoma in situ involves many ducts in REMOVED_DATE the specimen  There is a prominent lymphoid reaction to the tumor  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors 