Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  28 AUG 97 at 15 12 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma on core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA FORMING NODULES THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 33     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILA   The lymph nodes do not contain keratin positive carcinoma cells  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Re excision left breast cancer  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan pink fatty adipose tissue  with a suture on one side  called Dr  Briggs and was told the suture designates medial resection margin   The medial half of the specimen is inked in black and the lateral half of the specimen is inked in blue  Sectioning reveals an ill defined  firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  0 5cm from the closest margin  There was also an ill defined  firm and fibrous area  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm located at the medial resection margin  The entire nodule and the sections adjacent to the thick segment of the localization wire was submitted in cassettes A through E  Representative sections of the ill defined  fibrous area at the medial resection margin are submitted in cassettes F through J   From the most medial towards the most medial margin of this ill defined area  with F being the medial resection margin   Labeled  Left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm tan pink fatty adipose tissue  Multiple lymph nodes were dissected and submitted in cassettes K through O  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Karen Lisa Furie  M D  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_e