 with fat necrosis  The probable fat necrosis comes to 0 1cm of the black inked margin  Sectioning of the latter shows a similar hemorrhagic previous biopsy site with surrounding tan yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  The probable fat necrosis comes to 0 1cm of the new black inked margin  The former fragments are entirely as C E  and the latter as F G  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the opposite surface shows an opened REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm hemorrhagic cavity consistent with previous biopsy site  Sectioning reveals multiple silver metal clips  The fibrous cavity averages 0 1cm in thickness  and there are surrounding areas of tan yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  up to 0 4cm  The probable fat necrosis abuts the black inked margin  and the cavity comes to 0 1cm of the black inked margin  The remaining cut surface consists of unremarkable tan yellow adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as H K  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  JOSHUA B  KISH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SUPERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN PART B  BREAST  LEFT   SUPERIOR LATERAL MARGIN PART C  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN , Unchecked.
