men is entirely submitted as D F  The second fragment of tissue has a black suture along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal hemorrhage along the previous inked biopsy site  The cut surface consists predominantly of unremarkable tan yellow adipose tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as G J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan yellow homogeneous cut surface with no lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as K N  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT SUPERIOR  RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT ANTERIOR  RE EXCISION PART C  BREAST  FINAL SUPERIOR   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Darryl A Oble  M D   Ph D  Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed Out by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH MUCIN PRODUCTION AND CALCIFICATION  STROMAL MUCIN EXTRAVASATION  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH IRRADIATION  SEE NOTE  SEE TABLE   1 Note  The ductal carcinoma in situ is associated with abundant mucin production  mucin accumulation within the ducts  and extravasation of mucin into the stroma  The presence of extravasated mucin raises the possibility of the presence of invasive mucinous carcinoma  however  malignant cells are not identified within the extravasated mucin  The carcinoma resembles the one resected from the patient s right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor and progesterone receptor proteins will be reported in an addendum  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor Size  Involving 2 of 7 blocks and spanning at least 0 7cm Grade  3 Calcifications  Limited to the carcinoma in situ Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen and to less than 0 2cm from the inferior and lateral margins of the specimen  Stains For Receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received unfixed   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  which has a long suture designating the lateral aspect and a short suture designating the superior aspect of the specimen  The long axis of the specimen runs from medial to lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen consists of unremarkable firm  dense  white breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely from lateral to medial in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the lateral tip in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the medial tip in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received unfixed   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of breast parenchyma  The specimen is inked  The tissue consists of tan white slightly myxoid breast parenchyma  which is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fellow Review by Darryl A Oble M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells