rtion of breast tissue with three localization wires in place  The specimen is not oriented  but in correlating with the radiograph and wires  the possible anterior half of the specimen is inked black and the possible posterior portion of the specimen is inked blue  Note that this orientation is not certain  Sectioning of the specimen reveals yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue with interspersed areas of fibrosis and scattered small cysts measuring up to 0 2cm  There are two small clips adjacent to the thick segment of the three localization wires  The adjacent parenchyma is focally hemorrhagic and fibrous in areas  but no discrete lesions are identified  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior end margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma adjacent to the posterior clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of posterior breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma adjacent to the anterior clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of additional tissue and the anterior portion of the specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior end margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections submitted upon re examination of the specimen  Received are multiple containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  shaved margin caudad   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of unoriented fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  shaved margin cephalad  are two fragments of unoriented fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  un