st tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 AUG 93 at 09 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is one piece of unoriented fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrofatty tissue consistent with breast parenchyma  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan nodule with an ill defined border within 4mm of the inked resection margin  Representative section as frozen section  1  Remaining lesional tissue in A  Remaining breast as B through N  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Kane  MD PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
