Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 04 CLINICAL DATA  1  History of left breast invasive lobular carcinoma  2  Radiation induced chronic mastitis                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  NECROSIS AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 00                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 20 x 17 x 7cm left mastectomy specimen which includes an REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm skin ellipse  On the medial aspect of the skin ellipse is a 3 5cm areola which is surrounded by a centrally located slightly retracted 0 6cm nipple  10 0cm lateral to the areola is an REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm puckered area which is slightly erythematous  The epidermis in this region is thrown up into rugose folds which surround the centrally located puckered area  The under surface of the specimen is rough and irregular  Sectioning through the breast parenchyma subadjacent to the area of puckered scarring reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm cavity which is filled by tan to gray fibrinous and grumous debris  The cavity is surrounded by an irregular rim of pale tan fibrous tissue ranging in thickness between REMOVED_DATE and 1 0cm  There are multiple pale tan fibrous bands which radiate in a stellate manner around the biopsy cavity and extends to the closest inked surface which is found on the undersurface of the specimen  Sectioning through the remaining breast parenchyma reveals innumerable pale tan fibrous bands which encircle islands of pale yellow adipose tissue and extend to multiple inked resec