 R  with the cyst in Q  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY  NO DISCRETE MASS SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  NO FROZEN DONE  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Kristina Braaten  M D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  CLINICAL DATA  56 year old with extensive DCIS and multifocal infiltrating duct carcinoma  11 of 22 lymph nodes positive  now for mastectomy given positive margin  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  SEVERAL FOCI AROUND THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SPANNING  0 6 CM  AND LOCATED   REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN  SEE NOTE   FIBROADENOMA  NOTE  Unequivocal evidence of invasive carcinoma is not identified in this specimen  see prior report MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the axillary portion  The overlying skin measures REMOVED_DATE x 16 0cm with a REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple which is grossly unremarkable  A 6 0cm linear well healed horizontal scar is present at 10 o clock position which reaches up to 6 0cm from the nipple  1cm lateral to the first scar is a second 2 5cm well healed scar present in the upper outer quadrant  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm cavity which is lined by smooth to focally shaggy wall and which contains a blood clot  It lies 0 5cm from the posterior surface and 1cm from the anterior surface and corresponds to the overlying scar at 10 o clock position  A hemorrhagic tract which measures 4 5cm in length is present beneath the second scar and abuts the cavity and the overlying posterior surface  Small foci of orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis is present in and around the cavity and along the hemorrhagic linear tract  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows diffuse fibrous thickening with focal cystic change  No lymph nodes are identified in the axillary portion  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections from the biopsy  including closest to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections from the hemorrhagic linear tract  including closest to the posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section from the breast parenchyma where the cavity and the tract abut each other   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma away from the cavity  upper inner quadrant Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 38 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer on FNA outside hospital  reviewed at MGH                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND FOCALLY TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTERIOR  SUPERIOR  AND MEDIAL MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  UNREMARKABLE FAT  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY NODES   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  A FEW TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 20     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number and  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE lumpectomy specimen  inked as follows  black deep end superficial  red superior  medial green  lateral blue  inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm white mass grossly abutting the superficial and deep margins  Tumor and adjacent superficial margin are frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Tumor and adjacent deep margin is frozen as FX 2  FX 2 is submitted in cassette A  Section Code  B  tumor with superficial  deep and inferior yellow margin  superficial and is fatty   C  Anterior and deep tissue   superficial fatty   D  Tumor  superior  E  most lateral tissue  radial  F  Most medial tissue  radial  G  firm tissue  inferior  Labeled  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE in aggregate mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  submitted in cassettes H L  Labeled  additional left axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate mass of adipose tissue and tiny lymph nodes measuring less than 0 3cm each  Tissue submitted entirely in cassettes M N  Labeled  left breast additional superficial margin  is a nonoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of breast tissue cauterized on one aspect  submitted completely in cassette O  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1 AND  2  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA WITHIN A FRACTION OF A MILLIMETER FROM INKED SURFACE  MARGINS NEGATIVE  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  Eugene Francis Ruffolo  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST  EXCISION PART B  LEFT BREAST  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN PART C  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART D  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , Unchecked.
