y Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast 81 grams   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm skin containing a nipple and separate REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm ellipse of tan unremarkable skin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty breast tissue  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic area is present 0 3cm from the posterior margin  0 6cm from the anterior resection margin and 1 0cm from the remaining resection margins  The dense hemorrhagic area is submitted in cassettes A E  Sections from the area surrounding this hemorrhagic area are submitted in cassettes F J  Representative section of a stellate hemorrhagic area suspicious for previous biopsy site is submitted in cassettes K with adjacent deep margin  Representative section of fibrous tissue in L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast implant  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm implant  The specimen is filled with clear fluid and is inscribed with  McGhan 350cc   No soft tissue is attached  A gross photograph is taken  The specimen is for gross diagnosis only  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right left breast implant  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm implant  The specimen is filled with clear fluid and is inscribed with  McGhan 195cc   No soft tissue is attached  Gross photograph is taken  The specimen is for gross diagnosis only