Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  10 AUG 98 at 16 52 CLINICAL DATA  Diagnosis by core biopsy  invasive lobular carcioma  Long suture   lateral  short suture   short                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  DIFFUSELY INFILTRATING AN AREA OF ABOUT 10 CM IN GREATEST DIAMETER  INCLUSIVE OF THE CUTANEOUS DERMIS  AND PRESENT AT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN SIX OF SIX LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN FOUR OF FOUR LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  14 AUG 98 at 18 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast and axillary nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm tan white skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of axillary fat pad  There is a 1 5cm raised nipple  Adjacent to the nipple areolar complex is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm yellow purple discolored area  The specimen is oriented by the axillary tail and there is one long suture on the superior aspect  Sectioning through the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm firm  focally gritty  gray white to yellow fatty mass  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hemorrhagic focus within this mass  which is presumed to be the previous site of biopsy  This firm mass is within 0 3cm of the deep margin  0 7cm of the skin surface  and appears to abut the inferior margin  Sectioning through the remaining breast reveals predominately yellow fatty tissue with a small amount of gray white fibrous tissue and no other grossly appreciated masses  Several lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  ranging in size from 0 6cm to 2 1cm in greatest dimension and a representative section of each lymph node is submitted  SECTION CODE  A C  Firm  gray white mass to the deep margin  D   Mass to inferior margin  E F  Sections from area of hemorrhage within mass  G   Skin  H K  Lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axil