Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   95    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST MARGIN  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHATIC OR BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   5    HIGH GRADE  COMEDO TYPE  A FEW FOCI ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE TUMOR  AWAY FROM THE MARGINS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITHIN 3 OF 15 NODES  WITHOUT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  BREAST  RIGHT  ANTERIOR MARGIN   BIOPSY  ADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTERIOR MARGIN   BIOPSY  ADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 07     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     NOTE  Because of an apparent discrepancy between the size of the tumor measured radiographically  2 5 to 3 0cm   and the size of the invasive tumor recorded on the pathology report  the specimen is retrieved and an additional three sections are examined  X Z   A 3cm gross abnormality is identified  but it is composed histologically of a 1 5cm invasive component surrounded by proliferative fibrocystic changes and comedocarcinoma in situ  with a fibrotic periductal response   Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  excision right breast tumor   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast with a 1 5cm stellate  firm and gritty mass  located in the middle portion of the specimen  and 0 5cm from the anterior posterior margins  and away from all other margins  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  Section code  A B  tumor and anterior margin C D  tumor and posterior margin E  superior margin F  medial margin Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which 13 tan pink lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0 5cm in greatest dimension up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  Representative sections from each lymph node are submitted in cassettes G N  Note that a representative section from the largest lymph node has been bisected and entirely submitted in cassettes M N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right anterior margin  are 5 irregular portions of adipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Specimens are inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable parenchyma with no discrete lesions and they are entirely submitted in cassettes O T  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  posterior  are 2 focally cauterized portions of fibroadipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Both are inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable parenchyma  No discrete lesions are noted  The smaller portion is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette U  The larger portion is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette V W  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  ANTERIOR MARGIN    BIOPSY PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTERIOR MARGIN    BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
