ing assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lumpectomy specimen  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm ill defined nodule which lies within 0 1cm of an inked resection margin  Submitted entirely in A through I with lesion in A  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   NODULE SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
